---
description: Concept extraction, concept validation, and dependency ordering of definitions with cycle reports.
import:
  - plain_parser_base
requires:
  - resource_loading
---

***definitions***

- :ConceptTools: is the `plain_parser.concept_utils` module of :PythonApi:.

- :DefinitionItem: is one entry `{"markdown": ...}` of the `definitions` list of a :PlainSourceTree:, holding the text of one :Definition:.

- :ConceptGraph: is the graph whose nodes are concepts and which has an edge from concept A to concept B when the :DefinitionItem: of B mentions A, predefined concepts and self-mentions left out.

***implementation reqs***

- :ConceptTools: orders definitions with `graphlib.TopologicalSorter`: for each concept in :ConceptGraph: insertion order, the concept is added, then each concept defined in terms of it is added with it as predecessor; `static_order()` gives the concept order.

- :ConceptGraph: is built in :DefinitionItem: order: the concepts a definition defines are added first, then the concepts it mentions, each once.

- A :DefinitionItem: takes the position of the last concept it defines in the concept order; items are sorted in place by that position.

- :ConceptTools: lists cycles with `simple_cycles` of `plain_parser.graph` over :ConceptGraph:, keyed in definition order, with a limit of one more than the number reported.

***functional specs***

# extract-defined-concepts
:ConceptTools: extracts the concepts a :Definition: text defines and the errors found.
- The first `- ` followed by one or more comma-separated colon-wrapped names is read; each name that is a :ConceptToken: is a defined concept, in order.
- A name with another character gives `Syntax error: Invalid concept: {candidate}. Should contain only letters, numbers, hyphens and dots.`.
- A text without such a start gives no concept and the error `Syntax error: Invalid definition specification text: {text}. ...` of :ErrorMessages:.

# extract-used-concepts
:ConceptTools: extracts every :ConceptToken: a text mentions, in order, repeats kept.

# validate-concepts
:ConceptTools: validates the concepts of a :PlainSourceTree: and returns a list of error texts, empty when the tree is valid.
- First come the errors of every :DefinitionItem:, as extracted.
- A concept defined twice, or a predefined concept defined, gives one error `Syntax error: Concepts were defined multiple times: {concepts} .` naming them.
- Then each item of `implementation reqs`, `test reqs`, `functional specs` and `definitions`, in that order, gives `Syntax error: Concept {concept} is not defined in the definitions. {section}: {markdown}` for each mention of a concept that is neither defined in the tree nor one of :PredefinedConcepts:.

# sort-definitions
:ConceptTools: sorts a list of :DefinitionItem: entries in place so that every concept comes after the concepts its definition mentions.
- A list of zero or one item is left as is.
- Items without mentions keep their file order relative to each other.
- A definition of several concepts moves as one item.
- Mentions in nested sub-items count; self-mentions and :PredefinedConcepts: do not.

# report-concept-cycles
When :ConceptGraph: has a cycle, sorting raises `PlainSyntaxError` listing the elementary cycles, in the format of :ErrorMessages:.
- Each cycle is written `Cycle N: A -> B -> ... -> A`, where each concept is followed by a concept its definition mentions, starting at the earliest-defined concept of the cycle.
- Under each cycle line come the texts of the definitions on the cycle, in cycle order; a text that defines two concepts of the cycle is written once.
- Cycles are ordered by the definition position of their first concept, then by length.
- At most 10 cycles are listed; with more, the head says `Found more than 10 cycles` and `Showing the first 10.`, and the listed cycles are the ones whose concepts are defined earliest.
- A cycle is reported even when a definition on it also mentions an undefined concept.
